<div class="ld-sec" id="s1"><h2><span>1</span>Acceptance of these Terms</h2><p>These Terms and Conditions (the “<b>Terms</b>”) govern your access to and use of the website www.wizardlenzxrstudio.com (the “<b>Website</b>”) and of the training, development, consulting and digital products offered by Wizardlenz XR Studio (OPC) Private Limited, a company incorporated in India with its registered office in Madurai, Tamil Nadu and its operations in Chennai, Tamil Nadu (“<b>Wizardlenz</b>”, “<b>we</b>”, “<b>us</b>” or “<b>our</b>”).</p><p>By accessing the Website, submitting an enquiry, enrolling in a programme, commissioning a project or downloading any of our products, you confirm that you have read, understood and agree to be bound by these Terms and by our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/refund/">Cancellation and Refund Policy</a>, which form part of these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Website or our services.</p><p>Where you act on behalf of an institution or business, you represent that you are authorised to bind that organisation, and “you” includes that organisation.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s2"><h2><span>2</span>Our services</h2><p>Wizardlenz operates three service lines, each of which may be subject to additional written terms (such as a proposal, quotation, statement of work, programme brochure or licence agreement) that will prevail over these Terms to the extent of any conflict:</p><ul><li><b>Academy</b> — workshops, bootcamps, semester courses, faculty development programmes and in-plant training in extended reality (XR), including virtual reality (VR), augmented reality (AR) and related technologies, and in artificial intelligence (AI), including generative AI, machine learning and AI-assisted tools, delivered to institutions, organisations and individuals.</li><li><b>Studio</b> — design and development of XR training simulations, virtual showrooms, AR product experiences, VR event visualisation and other immersive solutions for businesses.</li><li><b>Originals</b> — our own games, XR experiences and developer tools (including ImmersiTest), distributed through the Website or third-party platforms such as itch.io.</li></ul><p>Descriptions on the Website are for general information and do not constitute a binding offer. We may modify, suspend or discontinue any service or feature at any time.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s3"><h2><span>3</span>Eligibility and accounts</h2><p>You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of majority in your jurisdiction, and legally capable of entering into a binding contract, to commission services from us. Individuals under 18 may participate in Academy programmes only through, or with the written consent of, a parent, guardian or their educational institution.</p><p>Where any part of the Website or our products requires an account or credentials, you are responsible for keeping them confidential and for all activity under them. Tell us promptly at <a href="mailto:inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com">inquiry@wizardlenzxrstudio.com</a> if you suspect unauthorised use.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s4"><h2><span>4</span>Enquiries, quotations and formation of contract</h2><p>An enquiry sent through the Website, by email or through our chat assistant is an invitation to discuss your requirements and is not an order. A binding agreement between you and Wizardlenz arises only when (a) we issue a written proposal, quotation, programme confirmation or statement of work and (b) you accept it in writing, by payment of the advance or fee, or by instructing us to begin.</p><p>Quotations are valid for the period stated in them (or 15 days if none is stated) and are based on the information you provided. If scope, dates, venue, participant numbers or technical requirements change, we may revise the price and timelines.</p><p>The chat assistant on the Website provides general information only. Nothing it says is a quotation, commitment, warranty or professional advice.</p></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s5"><h2><span>5</span>Fees, taxes and payment</h2><p>Fees are stated in Indian Rupees (INR) unless agreed otherwise and are exclusive of applicable taxes, including Goods and Services Tax (GST), unless expressly stated as inclusive. You are responsible for all taxes, duties and bank or payment-gateway charges arising from your transaction, other than taxes on our income.</p><ul><li><b>Academy:</b> fees are payable as set out in the programme confirmation or invoice, normally in advance of the programme start date.</li><li><b>Studio:</b> projects are typically billed in milestones (for example, an advance on confirmation and further instalments on defined deliverables). Each invoice is payable within the period stated on it, or within 7 days of issue if none is stated.</li><li>Overdue amounts may attract interest at 1.5% per month, or the maximum permitted by law if lower, and we may pause work or withhold deliverables until payment is received.</li><li>All sums are payable without set-off or deduction except as required by law.</li></ul></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s6"><h2><span>6</span>Academy programmes</h2><ul><li><b>Delivery.</b> Programmes are delivered on the dates, in the format (on-campus, in-plant or online) and for the duration agreed in writing. Institutions are responsible for providing suitable venue, power, network access, safe space for VR use and participant attendance, unless we agree to supply them.</li><li><b>Equipment.</b> Headsets, computers and accessories supplied by us remain our property. You are responsible for loss or damage caused by negligent or improper handling while in your custody, and we may recover reasonable repair or replacement costs.</li><li><b>Certificates.</b> Certificates of participation or completion are issued at our discretion based on attendance and the assessment criteria stated for the programme. We may withhold or revoke a certificate in the event of misconduct, plagiarism or non-payment.</li><li><b>Course material.</b> Slides, notes, projects, assets and software provided are licensed for the personal, non-commercial learning use of enrolled participants and may not be copied, recorded, resold or distributed without our consent.</li><li><b>Conduct.</b> Participants must follow instructions from our trainers and the host institution. We may remove any person whose behaviour is unsafe, disruptive or in breach of these Terms, without refund.</li><li><b>AI tools and content.</b> AI programmes may use third-party AI platforms, models and services that are governed by their own terms, which participants must follow. AI outputs can be inaccurate, incomplete or biased and should be reviewed before use. Participants must not enter confidential, personal or sensitive data into AI tools unless authorised, and remain responsible for how they use AI outputs, including compliance with copyright and academic-integrity rules. Access to third-party AI tools may change or be withdrawn without notice, and we do not guarantee their availability or accuracy.</li><li><b>Outcomes.</b> We commit to deliver the programme described; we do not guarantee employment, internships, grades, funding or any particular result.</li></ul></div>
<div class="ld-sec" id="s7"><h2><span>7</span>Studio projects</h2><ul><li><b>Scope and change requests.</b> Work is limited to the scope set out in the statement of work. Requests that go beyond it will be quoted separately and begin only on your written approval.</li><li><b>Client responsibilities.</b> You will provide timely access to information, content, brand assets, stakeholders, hardware and approvals. Delays on your side may extend timelines and costs, and we are not liable for resulting delay.</li><li><b>Review and acceptance.</b> Each deliverable is deemed accepted if you do not give written, reasonably detailed feedback within 7 days of delivery. We will correct material defects against the agreed specification within a reasonable period; this is your sole remedy for defects, other than a refund as set out in our Cancellation and Refund Policy.</li><li><b>Third-party materials.</b> Projects may use third-party engines, SDKs, fonts, models and stock assets under their own licences. Where you supply or select such materials, you are responsible for holding the necessary rights.</li><li><b>Portfolio.</b> Unless we agree otherwise in writing, we may describe the project and show non-confidential screenshots or footage in our portfolio and marketing, without disclosing your confidential information.</li></ul></div>
