<div class="ld-sec" id="s11"><h2><span>11</span>XR health and safety</h2><p>Immersive technology can cause discomfort in some people, including motion sickness, dizziness, eye strain, disorientation and, in rare cases, seizures in individuals with photosensitive conditions. Users should stop immediately if they feel unwell, take regular breaks, use XR only in a clear, safe space and consult a medical professional if they have any relevant health condition.</p><p>Headsets are generally recommended for users aged 13 and above (or as the manufacturer specifies), and younger participants must be supervised by a responsible adult. You are responsible for the safe use of equipment and the supervision of participants during sessions you host. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for injury or loss resulting from use that disregards these precautions or the manufacturer’s instructions.</p></div>
